                <pb facs="0138" n="64" xml:id="pg64"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Sanford to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 348]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 20, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch (confidential) No. 192, under date of the 9th instant, touching
                    the special mission to the United States.</p>
                <p>This government has not been led by me to expect, and I believe does not expect,
                    an extraordinary mission from our side in response to theirs, for I have taken
                    care to impress upon M. Rogier the difference in our usages in this respect; but
                    I have said, as a personal impression solely, that I presumed a suitable
                    response would be made to this special act of courtesy on the part of the King,
                    and that it would probably take a more formal character and channel than was
                    usual with respect to replies to letters of notification sent through a resident
                    legation.</p>
                <p>The extraordinary mission has departed, and sails, as I have before reported, on
                    the 24th instant from Liverpool. M. de Kerchove, who goes in the suite of Baron
                    de Beaulieu, is not, it seems, officially attached to the mission, as I have
                    been given to understand and had reported to you.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. J. SANFORD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
